| 1 | `x[i][j]` and `x[i]^2` are grammatical, but walk invokes a subscript followed by a subscript or a superscript without its first index: one index fails with `args = ()`, more silently give the wrong element | NEGATIVE-VERIFIED | implementation gap (walk) | `appendices/grammars/concrete-syntax.tex`, "Expressions"; `basic/operators/precedence.tex`, "Operator Precedence and Associativity"; `basic/operators/juxtameaning.tex`, "Juxtaposition" | none | astra, blinded, review | siblings: 84. Such a primary parses as a `MathPrimary` (not `SubscriptExpr`); its subscript goes to `evalAndInvokeMethod` (`interpreter/evaluator/Evaluator.java:1181`), whose `evalInvocationArgs` (`:1064`, `:1380-1381`) takes `exprs.subList(1,…)`, right for a juxtaposition list, wrong for a subscript list. `m[3,7]^2` prints `11449`, `(m[7])^2`, not `1075369` (probe `explorations/gap-ledger-probes/g02.fss`, in the parent of `e879b6a44`). The spec forbids only `x^2[i]`. Workarounds: `(x[i])[j]`, `(x[i])^2`, or bind first, as `explorations/apl/base/AplCore.fss:1859` does (`rk = rs[k]`). probe and full text: history, row 1 |
| 84 | a superscript or postfix operator may not follow a dotted access: `x.v^T`, `B.data^T`, `B.n^2`, `B.data^*`, and the same after a getter or a method call, give a bare `Syntax Error` at the `^` | NEGATIVE-VERIFIED | implementation gap (parser) | `Specification-1.0-frozen/appendices/grammars/concrete-syntax.tex:947-952`, "Expressions"; `Specification-1.0-frozen/basic/operators/juxtameaning.tex:137-142`, "Juxtaposition" | none | run-b, run-b2 | siblings: 1. `PrimaryItem` tries `LeftAssociatedPrimary` before `MathPrimary` (`ProjectFortress/src/com/sun/fortress/parser/Expression.rats:384-386`); `LeftAssociatedPrimary` (`:388-434`) admits `Subscripting*`, `ParenthesisDelimited*` and `Selector*` but no `MathItem`, and exponentiation is a `MathItem` (`:651-656`) that attaches only to a `MathPrimary` (`:463-465`), which a dotted form never becomes. A subscript after a dot works (`B.data[5]` = `15`). Workaround `(x.v)^T`. Probes `explorations/run-b2/probes/g4a_sub.fss` and five beside it (`g4a_base`, `g4a_getter`, `g4a_call`, `g4a_num`, `g4a_expop2`), in the parent of `22ea0cd90`. probe and full text: history, row 84 |
